        {
          "duration": {
            "from": 689.1999999999999,
            "to": 699.1999999999999
          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>On a cervical lymph node biopsy, a large binucleate cell with owl-eye morphology</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>On a cervical lymph node biopsy, a large binucleate cell with owl-eye morphology stains CD15-positive and CD30-positive. Which additional finding confirms this is a Reed-Sternberg cell of classical Hodgkin lymphoma?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>CD45 positivity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CD45 (leucocyte common antigen) is positive on surrounding reactive lymphocytes. Its presence would argue against a classical Reed-Sternberg cell.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>CD45 negativity</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Classical Reed-Sternberg cells are CD15+, CD30+, and CD45−. CD45 negativity distinguishes them from the surrounding reactive lymphocytes, which are CD45-positive.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>CD20 positivity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CD20 positivity characterises the popcorn (LP) cell of nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma, which is CD15− and CD30− — the opposite of classical disease.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>BCL-2 positivity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>BCL-2 overexpression is the hallmark of follicular lymphoma, driven by the t(14;18) translocation. It is not part of the Reed-Sternberg cell immunoprofile.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Remember: classical RS cells are CD15+, CD30+, CD45−. CD45 negativity separates them from normal lymphocytes. CD20+ with CD15−/CD30− defines the popcorn cell of NLPHL instead."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "The classical Reed-Sternberg cell triad is CD15+, CD30+, CD45−. CD45 negativity is the key discriminator separating the neoplastic cell from surrounding reactive lymphocytes."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
